<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech FinMin sets 5-yr bond auction at 11.30 pct.</title>
<headline>Czech FinMin sets 5-yr bond auction at 11.30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech Finance Ministry will auction five billion crowns ($179.7 million) in five-year state bonds with a maximum gross yield on bids at 11.30 percent on February 4, the Czech National Bank (CNB) said on Monday.</p>
<p>  NAME OF ISSUE:	    Bonds of the Czech Republic 1997-2002</p>
<p>  ISIN:			 CZ 0001000475</p>
<p>  ISSUER:		     Ministry of Finance CR</p>
<p>  AMOUNT:		     CZK 5 billion</p>
<p>  NOMINAL VALUE:	    CZK 10,000</p>
<p>  BOND TYPE:		  Bearer</p>
<p>  BOND FORM:		  Book entry</p>
<p>				  Central Securities Registry (SCP)</p>
<p>  ISSUE DATE:		 February 14, 1997</p>
<p>  MATURITY DATE:	    February 14, 2002</p>
<p>  MATURITY:		   Five years</p>
<p>  COUPON:		     Determined by multiple price</p>
<p>				  American auction as average YTM</p>
<p>  FREQUENCY:		  Annual</p>
<p>  EX-COUPON DATE:	   January 15</p>
<p>  INTEREST INCOME TAX:    According to the laws effective in</p>
<p>				  the CR:  25 pct witholding tax</p>
<p>MAXIMUM ACCEPTABLE</p>
<p>  YTM:			  11.30 percent, p.a.</p>
<p>  DEADLINE FOR BIDS:	February 3, 1997 1200 (1100 gmt)</p>
<p>  AUCTION DATE:	     February 4, 1997</p>
<p>ADMINISTRATOR OF ISSUE: Investicni a Postovni Banka a.s.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
